//api.github.com/users/ashleysommer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleysommer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleysommer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashleysommer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/gzip","state":"uploaded","size":1447035,"digest":"sha256:3b089fcfe82dccca2a9d560d88665ca0345f828b9cf21de554e611a55c2c7277","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-28T22:10:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T22:10:52Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/RDFLib/pySHACL/releases/download/v0.40.2/pyshacl-0.40.2.tar.gz"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RDFLib/pySHACL/tarball/v0.40.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RDFLib/pySHACL/zipball/v0.40.2","body":"- Oxigraph-backed validation no longer computes `len()` of the whole data graph for every validation result.\r\n  - `datagraph or sg` evaluated the truthiness of the DataGraph, which on Oxigraph runs a `COUNT` query over the entire store.\r\n  - Thanks @lepy\r\n- Plain string literals read from an Oxigraph store now compare equal to plain literals in the shapes graph.\r\n  - Oxigraph reports them as `xsd:string`; they are now mapped back to plain RDFLib literals, which fixes false violations of `sh:in`, `sh:hasValue` and similar constraints.\r\n  - Thanks @lepy\r\n- Add concurrency lock when adding system triples to the data graph, and only install the triples if they're not present in the graph.\r\n  - Thanks @mhatipog\r\n- Quick fix for when using PYSHACL_USE_FULL_MIXIN=1, the ontology mixer returns a plain Graph or Datagraph, not a wrapper.\r\n  - Better fix incoming next release from @AndreasEhstandLicenseofClarityLOC","mentions_count":3}